Python practices skill for Claude Code and Codex

This directory contains material adapted from the python-pro skill in
Jeffallan/claude-skills (https://github.com/Jeffallan/claude-skills), path
skills/python-pro, at commit 36f3fe8052da7c57083783268c6ea3265d075265
(release v0.4.20). That material is distributed under the MIT License,
copied in LICENSE.

The references are written fresh. They take in only the upstream examples
listed below, which the audit on cipherstash/skills#64 kept. Each example now
lives as Python source in examples/, with a test, where CI runs the Python
check suite over it. Defect numbers are the audit's.

Modifications in this copy
--------------------------

CipherStash made these changes:

- references/typing.md takes these examples from
  skills/python-pro/references/type-system.md:
  These five follow upstream's examples, which the audit found no defect in.
  Their names and docstrings are this project's own:
  - a Protocol with a class that satisfies it by its shape
    (examples/src/practices/protocols.py);
  - a TypedDict with a NotRequired key (examples/src/practices/records.py);
  - a builder whose methods return Self (examples/src/practices/builder.py);
  - an @overload whose return type follows its argument type
    (examples/src/practices/overloads.py);
  - assert_never for an exhaustive match
    (examples/src/practices/exhaustive.py).
  These four are fixed:
  - the ParamSpec decorator (examples/src/practices/decorators.py), fixed
    for D9: it is written in PEP 695 syntax, def logged[**P, R], with no
    TypeVar or ParamSpec declaration, which ruff's UP047 rejects at 3.12;
  - the generic Cache[K, V] (examples/src/practices/cache.py), fixed for D9:
    it is written as class Cache[K, V] with no TypeVar or Generic base,
    which ruff's UP046 rejects at 3.12;
  - the custom type guard (examples/src/practices/guards.py), fixed for D8:
    it returned bool, which narrows nothing; it now returns
    TypeIs[list[str]], from typing_extensions below Python 3.13;
  - the mypy configuration (the [tool.mypy] table in examples/pyproject.toml),
    fixed for D11: python_version is 3.12, not 3.11, and strict = true
    replaces the flags that strict already sets.
  Upstream's other type-system.md examples are not taken, so D6 (NumT bound
  to numbers.Number) and D7 (the type[MISSING] sentinel) leave with them.
  Every TypeAlias and TypeVar generic upstream writes is replaced by the
  PEP 695 rule (D9).
- references/errors.md is new, except the library logger that adds only a
  NullHandler (examples/src/practices/__init__.py), which follows the
  example in skills/python-pro/references/standard-library.md. The audit
  found no defect in it.
- references/checks.md, assets/pyproject-checks.toml, SKILL.md and the tests
  are new. Upstream's frontmatter metadata, persona, workflow, output
  templates, and links to skills that do not exist here are dropped.
